(2226814, 305910, 44242, '<td valign="top">Highlights blown out a bit. Good tip I heard is that instead of the sunny 16 rule, use the sunny 11 rule for shooting the moon. i.e. if using iso 200 film, set aperture to F11, and shoot at reciprocal shutter speed ( 1/200 sec). works well for me. Good luck in challenge.</td>', 'Highlights blown out a bit. Good tip I heard is that instead of the sunny 16 rule, use the sunny 11 rule for shooting the moon. i.e. if using iso 200 film, set aperture to F11, and shoot at reciprocal shutter speed ( 1/200 sec). works well for me. Good luck in challenge.', '2006-03-14 09:43:43.000000', NULL, 1),
