(2242745, 305935, 26045, '<td valign="top"><br/>god i was so uninspired!<br/> <br/>posty, all my choices sucked ahaha<br/>you, you fucking fuck<br/>did so well i could strangle you!<br/>bitch! aahahah<br/> <br/>my three commenteers: thanks!</td>', 'god i was so uninspired! posty, all my choices sucked ahahayou, you fucking fuckdid so well i could strangle you!bitch! aahahah my three commenteers: thanks!', '2006-03-20 20:46:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(2242853, 305813, 15711, '<td valign="top">I''m so glad this did well. I really love it!!!</td>', 'I''m so glad this did well. I really love it!!!', '2006-03-20 21:42:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(2242890, 305817, 42567, '<td valign="top">GREAT DOF!  The sun on the chest is a little blown, but I don''t think you can do much about that.  Maybe use the dodge/highlight tool 3%, that would darken the chest a little.  Its a great picture maybe a few more editing steps.  Burn tool to darken the background (helps the bird to stand out better) up the contrast +3 or +4, sel color (black/black +2, white/black +1, red/black +2) hue/sat (red/sat +4, blue/sat +2, master/sat +2). USM to help with the soft focus.  This is just me looking at the picture.<br/> <br/>Keep up the great work.  Believe me, your pictures/scores will get BETTER!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-03-20 22:08:39.</i></td>', 'GREAT DOF!  The sun on the chest is a little blown, but I don''t think you can do much about that.  Maybe use the dodge/highlight tool 3%, that would darken the chest a little.  Its a great picture maybe a few more editing steps.  Burn tool to darken the background (helps the bird to stand out better) up the contrast +3 or +4, sel color (black/black +2, white/black +1, red/black +2) hue/sat (red/sat +4, blue/sat +2, master/sat +2). USM to help with the soft focus.  This is just me looking at the picture. Keep up the great work.  Believe me, your pictures/scores will get BETTER!', '2006-03-20 22:03:33.000000', '2006-03-20 22:08:39.000000', 0),
(2242908, 305911, 37893, '<td valign="top">Please tell me your camera is dust free ;) Great job my friend ;)</td>', 'Please tell me your camera is dust free ;) Great job my friend ;)', '2006-03-20 22:11:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(2243020, 305665, 28710, '<td valign="top">:) Thanks.<br/> <br/>Strangeghost: There is a noble hope in this picture that others will have found books as fascinating as I have in my life.<br/> <br/>I grew up as an avid "DEVOURER" of books and many are the times when I felt like this inside over something I have read.<br/> <br/>I would hope that there are other literary sources that can make a person, be it a young male or otherwise that can extract a response that are somewhat more deep than a girlie mag or a peice of jewelry.<br/> <br/>As someone else who works in the education field (I''m an English teacher), one would hope that we might share the same hope that books themselves are worthy of such a reaction, and the book in question is different for each individual...<br/> <br/>Nonetheless, I''m grateful for your comment. Definitely something to learn from it... And that''s what I''m lookin'' for. :)</td>', ':) Thanks. Strangeghost: There is a noble hope in this picture that others will have found books as fascinating as I have in my life. I grew up as an avid "DEVOURER" of books and many are the times when I felt like this inside over something I have read. I would hope that there are other literary sources that can make a person, be it a young male or otherwise that can extract a response that are somewhat more deep than a girlie mag or a peice of jewelry. As someone else who works in the education field (I''m an English teacher), one would hope that we might share the same hope that books themselves are worthy of such a reaction, and the book in question is different for each individual... Nonetheless, I''m grateful for your comment. Definitely something to learn from it... And that''s what I''m lookin'' for. :)', '2006-03-20 22:59:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(2243031, 305619, 21724, '<td valign="top">Amazing photo!!!  Easily one of my favorites ever taken.. I love the detail on her face.. it''s so subtle, so it''s easy to overlook, but the lighting on it is just gorgeous. It looks so much like a painting, I''m just amazed. If this were a print I would buy it in a heartbeat.<br/> <br/>Two questions: Her right arm looks somewhat awkward.. almost like it''s double jointed.. At first glance it looks like her arm is bulging out, but obviously this girl is not fat so I don''t know how that could be.  Also, there seems to be a weird discoloration on her hip right above the cloth.  Is that a trick of the light, or is that a result of cloning, or what?<br/> <br/>Regardless, an incredible image.  It will always be one of my favorites.</td>', 'Amazing photo!!!  Easily one of my favorites ever taken.. I love the detail on her face.. it''s so subtle, so it''s easy to overlook, but the lighting on it is just gorgeous. It looks so much like a painting, I''m just amazed. If this were a print I would buy it in a heartbeat. Two questions: Her right arm looks somewhat awkward.. almost like it''s double jointed.. At first glance it looks like her arm is bulging out, but obviously this girl is not fat so I don''t know how that could be.  Also, there seems to be a weird discoloration on her hip right above the cloth.  Is that a trick of the light, or is that a result of cloning, or what? Regardless, an incredible image.  It will always be one of my favorites.', '2006-03-20 23:03:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(2243129, 305997, 29753, '<td valign="top">this is great, sin city is amazing and you did very well to capture it</td>', 'this is great, sin city is amazing and you did very well to capture it', '2006-03-20 23:40:41.000000', NULL, 0),
